{"name":"Niagara Falls","hex":"#cbe3ee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Niagara Falls","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A waterfall in Niagara river, Niagara region, on the international border between Canada and United States, in both Ontario and New York state; Massive waterfalls located on the Niagara River.","A city in Niagara County, New York, United States; near the Falls."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Niagara_Falls"}],"entries":[{"title":"Niagara Falls","blocks":[{"text":"Niagara Falls is a group of three waterfalls at the southern end of Niagara Gorge, spanning the border between the Canadian province of Ontario and the U.S. state of New York. The largest of the three is Horseshoe Falls, which straddles the international border of the two countries. It is also known as the Canadian Falls. The smaller American Falls and Bridal Veil Falls lie within the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/3Falls_Niagara.jpg/330px-3Falls_Niagara.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Niagara_Falls","wikidata":"Q34221"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Canadian_Horseshoe_Falls_with_city_of_Niagara_Falls%2C_Ontario_in_background.jpg/500px-Canadian_Horseshoe_Falls_with_city_of_Niagara_Falls%2C_Ontario_in_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Canadian_Horseshoe_Falls_with_city_of_Niagara_Falls%2C_Ontario_in_background.jpg/1280px-Canadian_Horseshoe_Falls_with_city_of_Niagara_Falls%2C_Ontario_in_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Canadian_Horseshoe_Falls_with_city_of_Niagara_Falls%2C_Ontario_in_background.jpg/500px-Canadian_Horseshoe_Fa